      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1325133564,
      "text": "Detarium microcarpum, commonly known as sweet detar, sweet dattock or tallow tree, is an underutilized species of tree legume that grows naturally in the drier regions of West and Central Africa. It has a wide range of uses due to its medicinal properties, edible fruit and hardwood, which is used as fuel. This makes it valuable and appreciated by local communities, but further research and effort are needed for its domestication."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Detarium microcarpum",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detarium_microcarpum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 222453011,
      "text": "Detarium microcarpum est une espèce de plantes à fleurs du genre Detarium de la famille des Fabaceae, que l'on trouve en Afrique de l'Ouest et du Centre."
    }
  },
